  "body": "A stock-source 2D Chamfer can post a cut into a part. This occurs when the part is added after generation and the program sim judges the stock.\n\n## Reproduction\n\nThe fixture of `crates/app/tests/stock_source_holes.rs` (`stock_source_chamfer_refusal_names_cause_and_part_as_source_workaround`, the \"chamfer-rejudge-hint\" case):\n\n1. Use `job(Model::hole(3.0, 8.0), HALF, rotated)` with `HALF = 35`.\n2. Generate a stock-source 2D Chamfer, `chamfer(1.0)`. The generation is clean.\n3. Import a part \"other\": a plate on x [30, 35], y [-5, 5], z [0, 20].\n4. Call `posting::post_setup`.\n\nResult on `main` at `7e26134bf`:\n\n- Stock aligned: `POSTED`. The program has `G01 X35. Y-35. Z19.` along the edge of \"other\".\n- Stock turned a quarter about Z: `POSTED` (the red case of #2306).\n- Stock turned 1e-6 rad about Z (the sim does not judge): `post blocked - ... S1 now cuts part 'other' (move 5 cuts past the finish surface (stock-source chamfer breaks into a part; ...`.\n\n## Cause\n\nIn `crates/app/src/posting_sim.rs`, `judge_clause` calls `kept_moved` (the live re-judge of #1628, `operation::kept_rejudge::moved_part_problem`) only in the `Err(reason)` arm, when the sim does not judge. In the `Ok(_)` arm with zero gouge cells, the re-judge does not run. The column sim does not see this chamfer cut into \"other\". Thus the post goes out.\n\n- The aligned case exists since #1628 (commit `329db7d80`).\n- #2182 (#2177) made the sim judge a quarter-turned box. Thus the quarter-turned case now also posts.\n\n## Proposed fix\n\nRun `kept_moved` also in the `Ok(_)` arm when the sim finds no gouge. Add a pinning test for the aligned and the quarter-turned stock. Then run each suite that posts, because the change can add refusals.\n\nFound during #2306.\n",
